---
// /prototypes/setup/funding-sources: the Funding sources milestone, as a walk.
//
// Answers to docs/product-brief.md § 5, for this screen:
//   WHO         Dana, the tenant admin, standing the program up alone or beside
//               the account team; later, program staff adding a grant mid-year.
//   DOING WHAT  Getting every fund the program draws on into the system, with who
//               administers it and, where one exists, its award, so a project's
//               funding table has something to pick from.
//   BRINGING    Grant agreements and an annual report; the names of their funders;
//               award figures for the big grants and none for donations.
//   OPTIMIZING  Confirming what the documents already said over typing it; one
//               question a screen; nothing lost between sittings.
//   PAYS FOR    The reference list. dbo.FundingSource rows, each with a name, an
//               administering organization and, where stated, a TotalAwardAmount.
//   LEAVES OUT  Commitments. See below.
//
// THE GOAL OF THIS STEP IS "WHAT ARE ALL THE GRANTS". Andy, 2026-09-18, on the
// one-page version that carried a commitments table and a notes field: "I want
// the goal of this funding step to be: what are all the grants ... individual
// data connections between a project and funding source feel like the ongoing
// maintenance and use of the platform." So this milestone configures the list
// and stops. A commitment (dbo.ProjectFundingSource) is entered on the project
// record, in its Funding sources card, and the note to support went with the
// wizard it came from.
//
// THREE SCREENS, IN START'S WALK. The documents' suggestions as tiles, one
// question over the whole cast; the funds the documents did not name, typed;
// the roster and the arrow to the hub. One question a screen is what Start
// established and what Andy asked for here ("make funding sources a multi-step
// thing"); the shell is firma2-setup-stepper and the screens are the three
// components below. The brief's "setup is not a wizard" (§ 4) still holds in the
// sense it meant: the page is resumable at its URL, the step rides the query
// string, Finish later keeps the draft, and no screen demands an answer to
// leave.
//
// THE CONTRACT WITH THE TEAMMATE'S SPECIMEN (2026-09-17, "Funding Opportunities
// Setup") is the record: FundingSourceName, OrganizationName and the proposed
// TotalAward on dbo.FundingSource. Its per-record screens, its save moment and
// its recap are the walk's three screens; its commitments and its note are out
// of setup for the reason above.
import SetupLayout from '../../../layouts/SetupLayout.astro';
import Firma2SetupStepper from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-stepper.astro';
import Firma2SetupFundingPicker from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-funding-picker.astro';
import Firma2SetupFundingAdd from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-funding-add.astro';
import Firma2SetupFundingRoster from '../../../components/setup/firma2-setup-funding-roster.astro';
import EsaBadge from '@esa/ecology/esa-badge.astro';

const stepIds = ['suggested', 'add', 'review'];
---
<!-- manifest:
  layout: stack(2xl)
  sections:
    - status counts  -> esa-badge   (two, slotted into the milestone band SetupLayout renders)
    - walk           -> firma2-setup-stepper
      - suggested      -> firma2-setup-funding-picker
      - add            -> firma2-setup-funding-add
      - review         -> firma2-setup-funding-roster
-->
<SetupLayout title="Funding sources" width="wide" milestone="funding-sources">
  <!-- The counts the screens produce, at the top of the page. Synced by the
       script below from the same draft the screens read. -->
  <span slot="status" data-part="confirmed-count"><EsaBadge value="0 confirmed" variant="secondary" size="sm" /></span>
  <span slot="status" data-part="review-count"><EsaBadge value="0 to review" variant="secondary" size="sm" /></span>

  <Firma2SetupStepper stepIds={stepIds}>
    <Firma2SetupFundingPicker />
    <Firma2SetupFundingAdd />
    <Firma2SetupFundingRoster />
  </Firma2SetupStepper>
</SetupLayout>

<script>
  import { listFundingSources } from '../../../lib/setup-draft';

  const confirmedBadge = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-part="confirmed-count"] .esa-badge__text');
  const reviewBadge = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-part="review-count"] .esa-badge__text');

  const sync = (): void => {
    const sources = listFundingSources();
    const confirmed = sources.filter((source) => source.status === 'confirmed').length;
    const toReview = sources.filter((source) => source.status === 'suggested').length;

    if (confirmedBadge) confirmedBadge.textContent = `${confirmed} confirmed`;
    if (reviewBadge) reviewBadge.textContent = `${toReview} to review`;
  };

  document.addEventListener('setup-draft-change', sync);
  sync();
</script>
